Make isoreg() set yc[0] before its early return on empty input.

isoreg() (src/library/stats/src/isoreg.c) allocates 'yc' (length n + 1)
and returns early for n == 0 before writing its single element, so
isoreg(numeric(0))$yc is whatever the recycled node held instead of
cumsum(c(0, y)) == 0:

    x <- lapply(1:1e5, function(i) 12345.5 + 0); rm(x); invisible(gc())
    isoreg(numeric(0))$yc
    [1] 12345.5

An uninitialized read of a live allocation, so ASan does not report it
(MSan would).  Set yc[0] before the early return.

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R), not
carried here.  Found by the mutation harness's plain-vs-gctorture
differential, not by a fuzz target.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #381, filed 2026-10-16.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/library/stats/src/isoreg.c
+++ b/src/library/stats/src/isoreg.c
@@ -38,14 +38,14 @@ SEXP isoreg(SEXP y)
     SET_VECTOR_ELT(ans, 2, yf = allocVector(REALSXP, n));
     SET_VECTOR_ELT(ans, 3, iKnots= allocVector(INTSXP, n));
 
+    /* yc := cumsum(0,y); yc[0] also when n == 0 */
+    REAL(yc)[0] = 0.;
     if (n == 0) {
 	UNPROTECT(1); /* ans */
 	return ans; /* avoid segfault below */
     }
 
     /* unneeded: y = coerceVector(y, REALSXP); */
-    /* yc := cumsum(0,y) */
-    REAL(yc)[0] = 0.;
     double tmp = 0.;
     for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 	tmp += REAL(y)[i];
